:0.5,"def_epa_per_play":-0.01764},{"week":6,"opponent":"NYJ","home":true,"pf":26.0,"pa":19.0,"off_snaps":67,"epa_per_play":0.01227,"pass_rate":0.4776,"pass_rate_neutral":0.54,"def_epa_per_play":-0.03686},{"week":7,"opponent":"CHI","home":false,"pf":24.0,"pa":30.0,"off_snaps":49,"epa_per_play":0.1845,"pass_rate":0.6531,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6,"def_epa_per_play":0.1951}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2024,"team":"TB","distance":0.6455,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"},{"season":2025,"team":"HOU","distance":0.6717,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Nick Caley"},{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.6876,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Klint Kubiak"},{"season":2022,"team":"DEN","distance":0.6887,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"LV","distance":0.6939,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Josh McDaniels"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"PIT","distance":0.1219,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"TB","distance":0.3524,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Todd Bowles"},{"season":2023,"team":"DAL","distance":0.358,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3673,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":0.445,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Patriots are 4-3 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 160 to 143. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 11th in EPA per play while the defense sits 19th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd lowest no-huddle rate in the league.","offense":"The Patriots offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd lowest no-huddle rate in the league. Drake Maye has run the passing game, with DeMario Douglas leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Patriots defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been sack rate, where it ranks 12th, and its weakest has been EPA allowed per rush, where it ranks 24th. Elijah Ponder leads the team with 5.5 sacks, and Christian Barmore has added 3 despite playing only 49% of the snaps. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of pass rushers that ranks 5th highest in the league.","special":"The Patriots have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 82% of field goals, which is about average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 19% of the money on the books. Their quarterbacks were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Drake Maye has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,784 yards. Targets have been spread around, with DeMario Douglas and Hunter Henry leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Rhamondre Stevenson and TreVeyon Henderson. On defense, Elijah Ponder leads the team with 5.5 sacks.","coaching":"Josh McDaniels is calling the offense and Zak Kuhr is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Buccaneers under Liam Coen and the 2025 Texans under Nick Caley. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Steelers and the 2025 Buccaneers under Todd Bowles.","trends":"The offense went from 1st in EPA per play in 2025 to 11th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 11th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 19th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 4% to 8%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}